.TH START\-MU2EDAQ\-CONTROLCENTER.SH 1 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-controlcenter 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh \- start the Mu2e DAQ Control Center kiosk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
.PP
.B start.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardized Mu2e control-room start script for
.BR controlcenter (1).
It activates the package virtual environment, probes for a usable
OpenGL context, launches the GUI in the background, waits for the TCP
status server to accept connections, and then sends one
.B ping
per configured status indicator as a health check.
.PP
.B start.sh
is a symbolic link to this script, kept for one release after the
rename; both names run identical code.
.B start.sh
is the historical name and
.B start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
is canonical \(em it is the name recorded in
.I apps.yaml
and the name symlinked into the shared
.I ~/controlroom/bin
area, where the unqualified
.I start.sh
would collide with every other DAQ package.
.PP
The script takes no options; all behaviour is controlled by the
environment and by
.IR config/controlcenter.yaml .
.SS Startup sequence
.TP
.B 1. Virtual environment
Aborts if
.I venv/bin/python
is missing or not executable, directing the operator to
.IR bootstrap.sh .
.TP
.B 2. GPU probe
.B QWebEngineView
is Chromium and needs a working GLX context.  A failure can be delayed
well past startup, so the script creates a minimal offscreen
.B QOpenGLContext
in a separate 10-second process first.  If that fails it exports
.B QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software
and
.B QTWEBENGINE_CHROMIUM_FLAGS
to force software rendering rather than let the app abort later.
.TP
.B 3. Launch
Runs
.I src/controlcenter.py
with the bundled config, backgrounds it, and writes the PID to
.IR controlcenter.pid .
.TP
.B 4. Readiness wait
Polls a TCP connect to 127.0.0.1:$CRS_PORT_CMD once a second for up to
15 seconds, failing early if the process dies.  On timeout it kills the
process and exits non-zero, so a hung start never leaves a half-running
kiosk.
.TP
.B 5. Indicator ping
Sends
.B controlcenter-send ping
once per indicator in the hard-coded list
.BR DAQ ", " Trigger ", " Misc ", " Storage .
.SH OPTIONS
None.  The script parses no arguments and ignores any given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/bin/python
Interpreter; must exist before the script will run.
.TP
.I config/controlcenter.yaml
Configuration passed to the application with \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
.I controlcenter.pid
PID of the launched GUI, consumed by
.BR stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_CMD
Status-server port.  Exported by
.BR crs-app (1)
or
.BR mu2edaq-app (1)
from
.IR apps.yaml ;
defaults to 9876 when unset.  The script re-exports it so the
application inherits it, and uses it as the port to wait on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The GUI started and its status server accepted a connection.
.TP
.B 1
The virtual environment was missing, the process died during startup, or
the status server did not come up within 15 seconds.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with the default port:
.PP
.nf
  ./start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
.fi
.PP
Start under the control-room port assignment:
.PP
.nf
  crs-app start controlcenter
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR controlcenter (1),
.BR stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh (1),
.BR controlcenter-send (1),
.BR crs-app (1),
.BR mu2edaq-app (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group.
